A command with two functions that call only each other, so with the marks
withdrawn they are one dead component with both as roots. A string literal
spells bravo's name, which makes its finding possible, and the component carries
its lowest root confidence, so alpha's finding would be possible too. The default
minimum withholds it, so the directive on alpha is dormant rather than in effect.

-- go.mod --
module example.com/app

go 1.27
-- deadset.json --
{"target": {"kind": "application"}}
-- main.go --
package main

func main() { println(len(names)) }

var names = []string{"bravo"}

//deadset:ignore DS1002 -- kept for the loader
func alpha() { bravo() }

func bravo() { alpha() }
